hetero: forced stems said as written, forced first

The heteronym table consults grammar; some words need no asking. A
forced entry names a stem: wherever the stem leads the token, the stem
is replaced by its annotation and the rest stays on as text, so one
entry says produce/produces/producing and candidate/candidates.
Checked before the heteronym table, which it shadows.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
